github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111432","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111432","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111432.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111432.patch","merged_at":"2025-10-10T15:37:54Z"},"body":"This fixes LibGodot shared_library build to work properly on Linux; there was unfortunately some missing functionality in the original PR, #110863.\r\n\r\nThere's two fixes here:\r\n\r\n* The -fPIC flag needs to be introduced during the platform `configure()` step so that modules will be built with it.\r\n* The x11 and wayland platform sub-modules shouldn't use `env.Object` because it doesn't have the correct flags attached to it; instead they need to be added to `linuxbsd/SCSub`'s `common_linuxbsd` array so that add_library, add_shared_library, or add_program can do the right thing. This basically just means that we need to return a path instead of an env.Object, but we do need to wrap it with a constant path to get the right complete filename. (There might be a cleaner way to do this.)\r\n\r\nI can untangle these into separate PRs if you'd prefer them separate, this is just how I wrote 'em.\r\n\r\nTo test, run `scons library_type=shared_library` on Linux. (Shared libraries tend to be the pain point.)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https: